        "label": "Fade live ink marks",
        "job": "Work out how visible each ink mark drawn live on a canvas or screen is at a given instant, so live marks fade instead of piling up, and when each is gone",
        "description": "Give now (the instant to look at, an ISO time or milliseconds since the epoch), fade ({ hold_ms, fade_ms }: how long a mark is fully seen, then how long it takes to go) and marks ([{ ref, created_at? }]). Answers marks, one per mark in the order given, each with opacity (1 until hold_ms has passed since created_at, falling in a straight line to 0 over fade_ms, 0 after), shown and gone_at (the ISO instant it goes, or null for a mark with no usable time, which never fades), and the counts shown and gone. It reads only what it is given: no clock is read, nothing is drawn, no mark is changed or deleted. Refuses an empty list, a mark without a ref, a now that is not a time and a hold_ms or fade_ms that is not a number of zero or more. The screen (show/GraphCanvas.tsx, show/AddressedMarkLayer.tsx and the mark toolbar) also lays a list out as linked cards, takes the pen and keeps each stroke; this run does none of that. Folding, shaping and erasing marks are the tool:see-the-ink-marks-on-a-space, tool:turn-a-drawn-stroke-into-a-mark-shape and tool:find-the-ink-mark-to-erase rows in tools/draw-ink-marks; exporting marks as a picture file is the ink block of tool:export-a-document-to-a-file.",
